Acts 26:1 , Paul, in the presence of Agrippa, declares his life from his childhood;
Acts 26:12 , and how miraculously he was converted, and called to his apostleship;
Acts 26:24 , Festus charges him with being mad, whereunto he answers modestly;
Acts 26:28 , Agrippa is almost persuaded to be a Christian;
Acts 26:31 , The whole company pronounce him innocent.
